#: inc/core/Admin/SiteHealth.php:518
msgid "Sitemap"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:692
msgid "Leave the users out of the sitemap of WordPress."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:693
#: inc/core/Admin/SiteHealth.php:518
msgid "Login errors"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:693
msgid "Give a failed login one message, whether the login or the password was wrong, on the login form, WooCommerce and XML-RPC; and a password reset one message, whether the account exists or not."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:696
msgid "Exposed surface"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:697
msgid "What the site answers and advertises beyond its pages, and what the browsers are told."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:699
msgid "Switch XML-RPC off"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:699
msgid "Refuse every call of xmlrpc.php. A bot tries hundreds of passwords in one call through it; Jetpack and the mobile app of WordPress need it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:700
msgid "Refuse pingbacks"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:700
msgid "Drop the pingback methods of XML-RPC and the header announcing them. A pingback makes the server fetch an address a stranger chose: the usual way to bounce a site into a denial of service."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:701
msgid "Refuse trackbacks"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:701
msgid "Answer wp-trackback.php with a refusal before it fetches anything. A trackback is a link notification any stranger can send; spam fills it, nothing recent uses it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:707
#: inc/core/Admin/SiteHealth.php:518
msgid "Security headers"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:709
msgid "Send X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy and a frame-ancestors policy with every response: the browser then neither guesses the type of a file, nor tells a third party the page it comes from, nor shows the site inside another. A header the server already sends is left alone."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:714
msgid "The server sends every one of them on its own: the setting has no effect."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: names of HTTP headers
#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:716
#, php-format
msgid "The server sends %s on its own; Gecka Security adds the others."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:721
#: inc/core/Admin/SiteHealth.php:518
msgid "HSTS"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:723
msgid "Tell the browsers to reach the site over HTTPS only, for six months. For a site that will keep HTTPS: once sent, a browser holds it for the whole six months."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:725
msgid "The server sends it on its own: the setting has no effect."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:728
msgid "File editor"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:728
msgid "Switch the theme and plugin editors of the admin off. A compromised administrator account would use them to put PHP on the server; installs and updates stay possible."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:731
msgid "Journal and statistics"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:733
#: inc/core/Admin/StatsView.php:476
msgid "Successful logins"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:733
msgid "Record each successful login in the journal, with the address, the way in and the roles of the account, application passwords included: where an administrator logging in from an unusual address shows."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:734
msgid "Unknown logins"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:734
msgid "Record the login of a failure even when it names no account, to see which names the bots try; a password typed in the login field is then kept too. Off, the journal keeps only the logins naming an account or a reserved name."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:735
msgid "Account changes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:735
msgid "Record in the journal every account created or deleted, every role set, added or removed, every e-mail address or password changed, with who did it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/core/Admin/SettingsPage.php:736
